{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4093695","formula":"BCr","hill":"BCr","elements":["B","Cr"],"composition":{"B":1.0,"Cr":1.0},"names":{"en":"Chromium(III) boride","ru":"Борид хрома"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chromium(III) boride, also known as chromium monoboride (CrB), is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula CrB. It is one of the six stable binary borides of chromium, which also include Cr2B, Cr5B3, Cr3B4, CrB2, and CrB4. Like many other transition metal borides, it is extremely hard (21-23 GPa), has high strength (690 MPa bending strength), conducts heat and electricity as well as many metallic alloys, and has a high melting point (~2100 °C). Due to these properties, among others, CrB has been considered as a candidate material for wear resistant coatings and high-temperature diffusion barriers.","ru":"Монобори́д хро́ма — бинарное неорганическое соединение металла хрома и бора с формулой CrB, жёлтые кристаллы, не растворимые в воде."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":82788,"mass":62.81,"charge":0,"smiles":"B#[Cr]","inchikey":"NUEWEVRJMWXXFB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"boranylidynechromium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-260","atoms":12,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[2.903,0.0,0.0],[0.0,7.798,0.0],[0.0,0.0,2.902]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":1.134,"z":2.176,"el":"Cr"},{"x":2.903,"y":1.134,"z":2.176,"el":"Cr"},{"x":1.452,"y":2.765,"z":0.725,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.393,"z":2.176,"el":"B"},{"x":2.903,"y":3.393,"z":2.176,"el":"B"},{"x":1.452,"y":0.506,"z":0.725,"el":"B"},{"x":1.452,"y":5.033,"z":2.176,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.665,"z":0.725,"el":"Cr"},{"x":2.903,"y":6.665,"z":0.725,"el":"Cr"},{"x":1.452,"y":7.292,"z":2.176,"el":"B"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.406,"z":0.725,"el":"B"},{"x":2.903,"y":4.406,"z":0.725,"el":"B"}],"bonds":[[3,10,1],[4,11,1],[0,5,1],[1,5,1],[2,